// blitzAwards — assemble the celebration queue for a finished battle.
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// THE BUG THIS EXISTS TO FIX
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// `HeadToHeadGame.jsx` called `detectNewAwards({ points })` with NO `badges`
// argument, so the sixth award family — registry badges — could not fire from a
// battle at all. Earn a Blitz badge by winning a battle and nothing popped; the
// badge turned up later on the stats page with no moment attached to it.
//
// The identical defect on the SOLVE path was fixed on 2026-09-03 (docs/bugs.md,
// "Every registry badge was structurally unannounceable"). That fix listed
// `HeadToHeadGame.jsx passed { points }` as part of the root cause but only
// repaired `Game.jsx`. This is the other half.
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// WHY IT IS ITS OWN MODULE
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// It is the one piece of the battle-finish path that is worth testing on its own:
// three independent sources, each of which must degrade without taking the others
// down, on a screen the player has already finished. Inline in the component it
// was untestable, which is exactly how it stayed broken.
//
// Dependencies are injected so a test can drive every failure branch without a
// network or a Supabase client. Production callers pass nothing.
import { detectNewAwards, readSolveOutcomeSources, planSolveBadgeAwards } from '@/game-flow';
import { apiClient } from '@/transport';

/**
 * Battle-point tier awards for a player who just won.
 *
 * ⚠️ TIER-AGNOSTIC BY CONSTRUCTION, and that is a ruling, not an accident.
 * David, 2026-09-04: no mode of battle mints a puzzle piece, and a win in ANY
 * tier pays the same battle point. So this function must never look at
 * `blitz_mode` — an Expert win is just a win. It also must never reach the
 * puzzle-piece economy: `points.puzzle` is deliberately absent below, so
 * `detectNewAwards` cannot cross a puzzle tier from a battle even if a future
 * caller passes one in.
 *
 * @param {number} wins the player's battle-win total AFTER this battle
 * @returns {Array<object>}
 */
export const battlePointAwards = (wins) =>
  detectNewAwards({ points: { prevBattle: wins - 1, battle: wins } });

/**
 * Everything this battle just earned, in celebration order.
 *
 * @param {object} args
 * @param {boolean} args.isWinner did I win — only a win can cross a battle-point tier
 * @param {string} args.userId
 * @param {object} [deps] injected for tests
 * @returns {Promise<Array<object>>} the celebration queue, in family order.
 *
 * ⚠️ IT NO LONGER RETURNS A `commit`. Recording is the DRAIN site's job now,
 * and it records the whole queue rather than the badges alone — the battle medal
 * this function produces was previously remembered by nothing at all. See
 * game-flow/announcedAwards.
 */
export async function collectBattleAwards({ isWinner, userId }, deps = {}) {
  const {
    getMe = () => apiClient.auth.me(),
    readSources = readSolveOutcomeSources,
    planBadges = planSolveBadgeAwards,
    pointAwards = battlePointAwards,
  } = deps;

  const awards = [];

  // 1) Battle-point tiers. Only a win increments the total, so only a win can
  //    cross a tier. A failed read costs the player their tier celebration but
  //    must not cost them their badges — hence the independent try.
  if (isWinner) {
    try {
      const me = await getMe();
      const wins = me?.['game_stats']?.blitzStats?.wins ?? 0;
      awards.push(...pointAwards(wins));
    } catch {
      // Non-blocking by design: this runs on a finished screen.
    }
  }

  // 2) Registry badges. Checked whether the battle was won, lost or tied — a
  //    badge can be earned by PLAYING (a solve count, a comeback, a streak), and
  //    gating this on a win is how those would silently never announce.
  try {
    const { stateById } = await readSources(userId);
    awards.push(...planBadges(stateById, userId));
  } catch {
    // Same contract: a dead badge read must not cost the player their tier award.
  }

  return awards;
}
