// battleDice — pure resolver for "which dice does battle puzzle `index` show".
//
// Both players in a two-player battle MUST race the identical puzzle at each
// sequential index. Two sources keep them in sync:
//   1. The stored `dice_sequence` array (a single shared DB row) — authoritative
//      while `index` is in range. This is also what the server-side re-verify
//      (submitBattleResult) re-solves against, so it stays the source of truth.
//   2. Past the array's end, a DETERMINISTIC seed derived from the battle's
//      shared UUID (`challenge.id`) + `index`, via `blitzDiceForIndex`. Both
//      devices hash the same string, so index N yields byte-identical dice.
//
// The bug this replaces: the old overflow path called `generateBlitzDice()`
// (per-client Math.random), so once past the stored array each device rolled its
// OWN puzzle and the two players diverged (reported at puzzle #11 when the
// sequence was only 10 long). See docs/bugs.md 2026-07-30.
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// WHY EXPERT CANNOT USE THE FALLBACK
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// `blitzDiceForIndex` is deterministic, which is all Easy and Challenge need: it
// keeps both devices on the same puzzle, and in those tiers ANY equation reaching
// 37 scores, so an arbitrary roll is always playable.
//
// Expert requires a PERFECT solve — all three power dice used correctly — and an
// unvetted roll carries no guarantee that a findable perfect solve exists. Dealing
// one would hand both players a puzzle neither can clear, in a race where the
// deck does not advance until someone does. That is a wedge, not a hard puzzle.
//
// So for Expert this returns `null` past the deck, and the caller ends the run.
//
// ⚠️ WITH A 250-DECK THAT PATH SHOULD NEVER RUN. The deepest player-side in all of
// production history is 61 solves (measured 2026-09-04 over 142 sides), and Expert
// throughput is strictly LOWER than Easy/Challenge because only perfect solves
// advance the index. `null` is an assertion boundary, not a designed ending — if
// it ever fires in production, that is worth alerting on. It exists because
// "practically unreachable" is exactly what the previous 250-length comment
// claimed, while 43 of 71 production battles were meanwhile running on a stored
// deck of 10 and players were reaching index 61 through this very fallback.
//
// Intentionally NOT re-exported from the barrel — HeadToHeadGame is the only
// caller (imports via './battleDice'), matching the intra-module helper
// convention used by challengeView.bucketChallenge / playerBattles.derive*.
import { blitzDiceForIndex } from '@/dice';
import { blitzRequiresPerfectSolve, resolveBlitzMode } from './blitzMode';

/**
 * Resolve the 7-dice roll for a battle puzzle at `index`.
 *
 * @param {{ id: string, dice_sequence?: number[][], blitz_mode?: string }} challenge
 * @param {number} index - zero-based puzzle index
 * @returns {number[]|null} seven integers 1-6, or `null` when an Expert battle has
 *   exhausted its vetted deck — the caller MUST end the run rather than deal an
 *   unvetted roll.
 */
export const nextBattleDice = (challenge, index) => {
  const sequence = challenge?.dice_sequence;
  if (Array.isArray(sequence) && index >= 0 && index < sequence.length) {
    return sequence[index];
  }

  // Past the vetted deck. Expert stops; the other two tiers ride the
  // deterministic fallback exactly as they always have.
  if (blitzRequiresPerfectSolve(resolveBlitzMode({ challenge }))) {
    return null;
  }

  return blitzDiceForIndex(challenge.id, index);
};

/**
 * Has this battle run past the end of its vetted deck?
 *
 * Separate from `nextBattleDice` so a caller can ask the question without also
 * asking for dice — the resume path needs to know before it decides what screen
 * to show.
 *
 * @param {{ dice_sequence?: number[][] }} challenge
 * @param {number} index
 * @returns {boolean}
 */
export const isPastDeck = (challenge, index) => {
  const sequence = challenge?.dice_sequence;
  return !Array.isArray(sequence) || index >= sequence.length;
};
